---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
const title = 'Keeping Open Source AI Open'
const description =
	'HAIEF - The Human & AI ElevAItion Foundation builds open governance standards for human-safe, community-driven AI'
const discussions = 'https://github.com/NeuroLift-Technologies/haief/discussions'
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
	<!-- Crisis Banner -->
	<section class="crisis-banner" role="alert" aria-label="Breaking governance crisis">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="crisis-banner__inner">
				<span class="crisis-banner__badge">The Third Pillar</span>
				<div class="crisis-banner__content">
					<h2 class="crisis-banner__title">
						Anthropic is one evidence point in a broader governance gap.
						This is why Terms of Interaction exists.
					</h2>
					<p class="crisis-banner__text">
						The source-reviewed Anthropic case study tracks verified claims and TODOs separately.
						The strategic lesson is not that one company is good or bad. It is that companies
						mediating AI-human relationships need relational governance, continuity duties,
						transparency, consent, and user standing.
					</p>
					<a href="/case-study-anthropic-pentagon-2026/" class="crisis-banner__link">
						Read the source-reviewed case study &rarr;
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Hero Section -->
	<section class="hero hero--dark">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="hero__content">
				<span class="hero__eyebrow">The Third Pillar of AI Governance</span>
				<h1 class="hero__title">Keeping Open Source AI Open</h1>
				<p class="hero__subtitle">
					Big Tech is capturing open source AI governance. Without a people's counterweight, "open
					source AI" becomes a label that fails to deliver user empowerment. HAIEF completes the AI
					governance trilogy as the voice of users, communities, and democratic values.
				</p>
				<div class="btn-group">
					<a href="/take-action/" class="btn btn--accent btn--large">Join the Movement</a>
					<a href="/the-problem/" class="btn btn--outline-light btn--large">Understand the Crisis</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The Problem Preview -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section__header">
				<h2 class="section__title">Open Source AI Is Being Captured</h2>
				<p class="section__subtitle">
					The window for shaping AI governance is closing. Defaults are hardening right now.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid--3">
				<div class="card">
					<div class="card__icon">&#9888;</div>
					<h3 class="card__title">Corporate-Dominated Foundations</h3>
					<p class="card__text">
						The Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF) launched under Linux Foundation with 247 member
						organizations setting technical standards for agentic AI. Users have no equivalent voice
						in governance.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<div class="card__icon">&#128274;</div>
					<h3 class="card__title">The Licensing Gap</h3>
					<p class="card__text">
						Open source licenses protect code freedom, but AI creates new challenges: training data
						rights, interaction governance, multi-agent coordination. Current frameworks leave users
						unprotected.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<div class="card__icon">&#9203;</div>
					<h3 class="card__title">The Window Is Closing</h3>
					<p class="card__text">
						EU AI Act transparency obligations took effect August 2, 2026. OSI Open Source AI
						Definition 1.0 released. AAIF now has 247 member organizations. These structures are
						being built — but none include an explicit layer for human sovereignty.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-8);">
				<a href="/the-problem/" class="btn btn--primary">Read the Full Analysis</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The Solution -->
	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section__header">
				<h2 class="section__title">We're Not Competing. We're Completing.</h2>
				<p class="section__subtitle">
					HAIEF provides the missing pillar: human rights, public interest, and user sovereignty in
					AI governance.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="stats stats--alt" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number">66+</div>
					<div class="stat__label">GitHub repositories governed</div>
				</div>
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number">Live</div>
					<div class="stat__label">Deployed on Cloudflare Workers</div>
				</div>
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number">MCP</div>
					<div class="stat__label">Governance exposed as MCP tools</div>
				</div>
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number">v1.0.3</div>
					<div class="stat__label">OTOI governance contract active</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid--3">
				<div class="card">
					<h3 class="card__title">AAIF (Linux Foundation)</h3>
					<p class="card__text">
						Technical interoperability standards. Corporate-led. Essential for infrastructure.
					</p>
					<p><strong>Focus:</strong> How AI systems work together</p>
					<p
						style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-text-light); margin-top: var(--space-3); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
					>
						<strong>During the crisis:</strong> Technical standards are irrelevant when a government
						demands unrestricted access to AI capabilities.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="card">
					<h3 class="card__title">AI Alliance</h3>
					<p class="card__text">
						Open innovation and research. Academia + Industry. Advancing the science.
					</p>
					<p><strong>Focus:</strong> What AI can do</p>
					<p
						style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-text-light); margin-top: var(--space-3); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
					>
						<strong>During the crisis:</strong> Research alliances don't address the power dynamics
						between states, corporations, and users.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="card" style="border: 2px solid var(--color-primary);">
					<h3 class="card__title" style="color: var(--color-primary);">HAIEF (This Movement)</h3>
					<p class="card__text">
						Human rights, user sovereignty, community governance. People-led. Protecting users.
					</p>
					<p><strong>Focus:</strong> Who AI serves</p>
					<p
						style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-text-light); margin-top: var(--space-3); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
					>
						<strong>During the crisis:</strong> The only pillar that addresses who AI serves and
						provides community governance that survives state coercion.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The Solidarity Framework -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section__header">
				<h2 class="section__title">The Solidarity Framework</h2>
				<p class="section__subtitle">
					Open, community-driven governance for human-safe, emotionally-continuous AI
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="framework-diagram">
				<div class="framework-layer framework-layer--constitutional">
					<div class="framework-layer__title">Constitutional Layer (Governance Frameworks)</div>
					<div class="framework-components">
						<div class="framework-component">
							<div class="framework-component__name">TOI - Terms of Interaction</div>
							<p class="framework-component__desc">
								User's bill of rights. Declares preferences, boundaries, and requirements for AI
								interactions.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="framework-component">
							<div class="framework-component__name">OTOI - Orchestrated Terms of Interaction</div>
							<p class="framework-component__desc">
								Machine-side enforcement. Ensures AI systems respect and implement user TOI
								declarations.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="framework-layer framework-layer--protective">
					<div class="framework-layer__title">Protective Layer (Operational Protocols)</div>
					<div class="framework-components">
						<div class="framework-component">
							<div class="framework-component__name">RRT AIdvocAIte</div>
							<p class="framework-component__desc">
								Crisis intervention and emotional continuity. Multi-persona support for vulnerable
								users.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="framework-component">
							<div class="framework-component__name">Sleepwalker Protocol</div>
							<p class="framework-component__desc">
								Behavioral change protection. Preserves user agency during emotional or cognitive
								changes.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-6);">
				<a href="/solidarity-framework/" class="btn btn--primary">Explore the Framework</a>
				<a href="/why-ai-governance-must-be-open-adoptable-and-human-sovereign/" class="btn btn--outline btn--large" style="margin-left: var(--space-3);">Read the Manifesto &rarr;</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Why It Matters -->
	<section class="section section--dark">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section__header">
				<h2 class="section__title">This Is the Window</h2>
				<p class="section__subtitle">
					The open source community saved software freedom once. Now we need to save it again for AI.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div
				class="callout callout--danger"
				style="max-width: var(--container-narrow); margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);"
			>
				<p class="callout__title">Real-World Impact</p>
				<p>
					Vulnerable users face abandonment when AI sessions end. Crisis intervention gaps leave
					people at risk. <strong>This isn't theoretical. Lives are at stake.</strong>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="stats">
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number" style="color: white;">40+</div>
					<div class="stat__label" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">
						State AGs investigating AI harms
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number" style="color: white;">2026</div>
					<div class="stat__label" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">
						EU AI Act transparency obligations active
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number" style="color: white;">247</div>
					<div class="stat__label" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">
						AAIF member organizations
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="stat">
					<div class="stat__number" style="color: white;">1.0</div>
					<div class="stat__label" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">OSI Open Source AI Definition released</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Who We Are Preview -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="grid grid--2" style="align-items: center;">
				<div>
					<h2>Public Infrastructure, Not Private Power</h2>
					<p>
						HAIEF is a community-driven initiative to embed user sovereignty in the licensing and
						governance infrastructure of open source AI. We're not building another corporate
						foundation. We're building a movement.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Community-owned</strong> - Not controlled by any single vendor</li>
						<li><strong>Technically proven</strong> - Built on working implementations</li>
						<li><strong>"Nothing About Us Without Us"</strong> - Neurodivergent community leadership</li>
						<li><strong>Open standards</strong> - Transparent, auditable, enforceable</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						<a href="/who-we-are/" class="btn btn--outline">Learn About Our Mission</a>
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="callout callout--info">
					<p class="callout__title">Founding Contribution</p>
					<p>
						HAIEF frameworks originated from NeuroLift Technologies LLC, founded by Joshua
						Dorsey Sr. These frameworks are being contributed to the public commons as shared
						infrastructure under community governance — to ensure AI governance serves everyone,
						not just those who can afford private development.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Call to Action -->
	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section__header">
				<h2 class="section__title">Join the Movement</h2>
				<p class="section__subtitle">Every voice matters. Every contribution counts.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid--4">
				<div class="card">
					<h4 class="card__title">Developers</h4>
					<p class="card__text">
						Contribute to framework implementation. Build compliant tools. Join working groups.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h4 class="card__title">Standards Bodies</h4>
					<p class="card__text">
						Help define Open Source AI with user sovereignty. Extend principles to interaction
						governance.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h4 class="card__title">Organizations</h4>
					<p class="card__text">
						Partner for strategic alignment. Early adopter advantage. Enterprise compliance.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h4 class="card__title">Users</h4>
					<p class="card__text">
						Understand your rights. Demand TOI compliance. Share your experiences.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-8);">
				<a href="/take-action/" class="btn btn--accent btn--large">Take Action Now</a>
				<a href={discussions} class="btn btn--outline btn--large" style="margin-left: var(--space-4);">
					Join the Discussion
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Key Messages -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container container--narrow">
			<blockquote
				style="font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); text-align: center; border: none; padding: var(--space-8); background: none;"
			>
				"Open source needs open governance. The community that built software freedom must now build
				interaction freedom."
			</blockquote>

			<div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-8);">
				<p style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); color: var(--color-text-muted);">
					Join us. Build with us. Govern with us.
				</p>
				<p style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
					<a href="/questions-and-answers/" class="btn btn--outline">Browse Q&amp;A</a>
					<a href="/submit-question/" class="btn btn--outline" style="margin-left: var(--space-3);">
						Ask a Question
					</a>
					<a href="/submit-fact-check/" class="btn btn--outline" style="margin-left: var(--space-3);">
						Submit Fact-Check
					</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
